<item><title>South Africa braces for storms before a drier El Niño summer</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/south-africa-braces-for-storms-before-a-drier-el-nino-summer-b6e15b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/south-africa-braces-for-storms-before-a-drier-el-nino-summer-b6e15b/</guid><category>South Africa</category><description>Forecasters say thunderstorms are due over the Free State and Gauteng, and temperatures will climb to 32ºC-36ºC once the cloud over the interior clears.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:20:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" length="36666" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>South African public schools expect fee increases of up to 10% in 2027</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/south-african-public-schools-expect-fee-increases-of-up-to-b11282/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/za/south-african-public-schools-expect-fee-increases-of-up-to-b11282/</guid><category>South Africa</category><description>Fedsas says some schools are forecasting increases of 12% to 15%, as families already cut grocery spending and use savings to pay education costs.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:14:19 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" length="36666" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/za.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
